<title>UK: TransCo UK gas statistics for Feb 6.</title>
<headline>TransCo UK gas statistics for Feb 6.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransCo, the pipeline division of British Gas plc, has announced the following forecasts and data for gas use in the period February 4-6.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>Feb 4 (actual) 306 million cubic metres, 72 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Feb 5 (forecast) 308 million cubic metres, 72 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Feb 6 (forecast) 303 million cubic metres, 71 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Feb 4 (actual) 6.4 Celsius, seasonal normal 3.9 Celsius</p>
<p>Feb 5 (forecast) 5.1 Celsius, seasonal normal 4.0 Celsius</p>
<p>Feb 6 (forecast) 8.2 Celsius, seasonal normal 4.0 Celsius</p>
<p>There were no interruptions in any of the 13 Local Distribution Zones (LDZs) on Wednesday. TransCo forecasts a &quot;low&quot; probability of interruption in all LDZs on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
